rked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x-2x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x+2x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(11x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)-\\frac{1}{22}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(11x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340468/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a371de4-7c3f-5687-bd3a-d3ab5ab803ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340474/field-1/b58bcd4b6de53aa2ccb1c0cd9f5b5e5e93dd16e72fa0425cd55a93d0749b8734" :answer/id #uuid "fd2701b2-0251-53dd-b393-c479818feb86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340474/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9e2b4f9-6257-59dc-b0a2-74818df9ecbf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340474/field-1/b58bcd4b6de53aa2ccb1c0cd9f5b5e5e93dd16e72fa0425cd55a93d0749b8734" :answer-field/choices ["q-340474/field-1/b58bcd4b6de53aa2ccb1c0cd9f5b5e5e93dd16e72fa0425cd55a93d0749b8734"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340474" :question/id #uuid "b5544c7c-d4d3-583d-a4bf-b5627cabeed4" :question/math-academy-id "q-340474" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the second equation from the first, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x-3x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x+3x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)-\\frac{1}{20}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{20}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(0-0)-\\frac{1}{20}(1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340474/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a371de4-7c3f-5687-bd3a-d3ab5ab803ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340474"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340489/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "0eee9ee8-c198-5308-b016-f88f3f990c90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340489/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0bae5a0-f5b6-58ee-97de-cd1c217b51fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340489/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer-field/choices ["q-340489/field-1/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340489" :question/id #uuid "fce53d9e-1d44-575e-8af4-56b946eb770f" :question/math-academy-id "q-340489" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x+3x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x-3x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{24}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{24}(1-1)-\\frac{1}{12}(-1-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340489/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340489"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340492/field-1/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" :answer/id #uuid "c8f01ba5-3e32-5555-b13b-095531acef59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340492/field-1/29f1bd004b0e742e8153de2e3a77945bac059aed56c8ead2bc0011a45597d328" :answer/id #uuid "191e24b8-1848-5c3c-bfa9-c7909dcbba7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340492/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "19eee36c-9bd6-5baa-809d-d3073c43a866" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340492/field-1/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" :answer-field/choices ["q-340492/field-1/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" "q-340492/field-1/29f1bd004b0e742e8153de2e3a77945bac059aed56c8ead2bc0011a45597d328"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340492" :question/id #uuid "8f1b9c1a-1da5-5dd5-bb7d-543d04c36f2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-340492" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x+x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x-x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{16}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)-\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)]}_{0}^{3\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}(1-1)-\\frac{1}{12}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340492/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9d3b7f35-fcd1-5443-b0ea-0b06e016e0c3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340492"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340484/selection/e2740158477cab96f43cb6bba1b677066c6595765fd13e5f59e1b40b1845fb29" :answer/id #uuid "794e88a4-0240-54da-862e-f4d475966cc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{28}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(14x)-\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340484/selection/e31571f466d8e263b14ebaca4edb78a6c6b31826ea232cd35ae99312be980a39" :answer/id #uuid "07b97bea-b900-570b-ab55-02ce2ebf1a7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{28}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(14x)+\\frac{1}{48}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340484/selection/c8f459e35b3a3583608e0c71173c2d5602b0046e9161568e70eff3e24777c094" :answer/id #uuid "2b5de101-e156-5144-a1ae-befc0065889e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{28}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(13x)+\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340484/selection/8127e6e39308fa2e6253560c6da8db4980a3aa33abe9d91642028f727fe2f788" :answer/id #uuid "84c1e8ed-3496-561f-b1c4-a9f023fd5571" :answer/type :answer.type/m